From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 14:42:52 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 15/42] transports/lib+handlers: AdminAuthz stub +
 tenant-scoped admin middleware
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Foundation for the per-tenant admin interface. Defines a small AdminAuthz
interface for resolving the calling identity into (callerTenant,
isPlatformAdmin) so each admin handler can scope its DB reads/writes
correctly. v1 ships StubPlatformAdminAuthz which treats every caller as a
platform-admin whose own tenant is DefaultTenantID (overridable via
BIFROST_ADMIN_DEFAULT_TENANT); Phase 4's OIDC-backed AuthzPlugin replaces
this in place.

Three middlewares for the admin route tree:

- RequireTenantPathMiddleware(authz) — for the new
  /api/tenants/{tenant_id}/... route family. Reads {tenant_id} from the
  fasthttp URL param, authorizes via AdminAuthz (only platform-admin can
  target a tenant other than their own), and lifts the resolved tenant id
  onto ctx under multitenant.BifrostContextKeyTenantID. Tenant-admin
  cross-tenant attempts get 403.

- LegacyAdminTenantScopeMiddleware(authz) — for the existing /api/<entity>
  routes. Lifts the caller's own tenant id (from AdminAuthz) onto ctx so
  the same handler code automatically scopes tenant-admins to their own
  data. Empty caller falls back to DefaultTenantID.

- RequirePlatformAdminMiddleware(authz) — for /api/platform/*. Rejects
  any caller that is not a platform-admin.

Also adds multitenant.DefaultTenantID = "default" so call sites in
lib/handlers don't have to import framework/configstore/tables just for
the literal.

Patch ships the middleware + AdminAuthz only; subsequent patches enforce
tenant_id scoping inside the existing admin handlers (providers, MCP,
governance entities) and add the parallel /api/tenants/{tid}/... routes.

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
